    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as the clear cornerstone of the lineup, boasting a formidable 82.13 efficiency score. His matchup against Junk is highly favorable, bolstered by a 16% SP skill advantage and a critical 14% boost from a dynamic platoon split. Batting out of the leadoff spot, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary source of speed today, as his projection is further elevated by the specific weighting we place on stolen base potential. While **Yordan Alvarez** (60.70) remains an automatic start due to his elite 0.442 xwOBA, he faces a stiffer challenge against Gilbert; however, his lineup position and platoon advantage ensure he remains a vital anchor for our run production. We are also monitoring **Hector Rodriguez** (60.91), who benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Ritchie, effectively masking the drag created by his bottom-third spot in the batting order.\n\nOur bench decisions were primarily dictated by the absence of **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, both of whom are sidelined due to rainouts, alongside the existing IL status of **Colt Keith** and the absence of **Lars Nootbaar**. The most difficult start/sit decision involved **Trea Turner** (59.07) and **Junior Caminero** (58.47). While **Trea Turner** provides high-end utility, he is currently being suppressed by a tough matchup against May and a wind-in factor that lowers his HR probability. **Junior Caminero** came within inches of displacing others in the outfield, but the difficulty of facing Fried ultimately kept his efficiency just below the 60-point threshold for an elite designation. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Carson Benge** (44.39); his lineup is still pending, and should he fall out of the #5 spot, his L/L platoon disadvantage against Gore will make him a liability compared to depth options like **Gary Sanchez** or **Josh Smith** if we need a late-game pivot.",
